1
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,940
- You swear it? - By the Mother.

2
00:02:13,410 --> 00:02:16,540
My son has no interest in the Iron Throne.

3
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:25,140
Then I see no reason for hostility between us.

4
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,830
Your son can go on calling himself King in the North,

5
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:32,420
The Starks will have dominion over all lands north of Moat Cailin,

6
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:34,710
provided he swears me an oath of fealty.

7
00:02:34,710 --> 00:02:35,860
And the wording of this oath?

8
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:38,890
The same Ned Stark swore to Robert 18 years ago.

9
00:02:40,510 --> 00:02:44,380
Cat, their friendship held the kingdoms together.

10
00:02:49,050 --> 00:02:51,600
And in return for my son's loyalty?

11
00:02:51,890 --> 00:02:54,470
In the morning I'll destroy my brother's army.

12
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:56,730
When that's done,

13
00:02:56,980 --> 00:03:00,610
Baratheon and Stark will fight their common enemy together,

14
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:02,900
as they have done many times before.

15
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:11,980
Our two houses have always been close,

16
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:16,250
which is why I am begging you to reconsider this battle.

17
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:18,020
Negotiate a peace with your brother.

18
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:19,850
Negotiate with Stannis?

19
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,170
You heard him out there.

20
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:25,230
I'd have better luck debating the wind.

21
00:03:27,170 --> 00:03:29,090
Please bring my terms to your son.

22
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:32,200
I believe we are natural allies.

23
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,840
I hope he feels the same.

24
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:36,980
Together we could end this war in a fortnight.

25
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:52,840
No!

26
00:03:57,310 --> 00:03:59,320
- No. - Follow me!

27
00:04:02,050 --> 00:04:05,570
- You'll die for this. - No, wait, it wasn't her!

28
00:04:49,630 --> 00:04:51,180
We've got to leave.

29
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:54,940
They'll hang you for this.

30
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,350
- Inside the king's tent, go! - Now!

31
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:01,000
I won't leave him.

32
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:05,230
You can't avenge him if you're dead.

33
00:05:06,330 --> 00:05:08,780
Over there, go!

34
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,180
Not that way.

35
00:05:44,970 --> 00:05:46,690
We need to go home.

36
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:50,290
- Loras. - My Lord, My Lady.

37
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:51,610
Get out.

38
00:05:51,610 --> 00:05:53,540
Stannis will be here in an hour.

39
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:56,640
When he arrives, Renly's bannermen will flock to him.

40
00:05:56,860 --> 00:05:58,930
Your former companions will fight for the privilege

41
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:01,050
of selling you to their new king.

42
00:06:01,470 --> 00:06:03,220
And you want that privilege for yourself.

43
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:05,990
You will note that I am standing here talking to you,

44
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:09,190
- not Stannis. - There's no time for this.

45
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,800
Ride back to Highgarden, sister.

46
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,580
I'm not running from Stannis.

47
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,250
Brienne of Tarth murdered Renly.

48
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:17,570
I don't believe that. You don't believe that.

49
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:21,410
Who gained the most from our king's death?

50
00:06:21,470 --> 00:06:23,070
Stannis.

51
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,630
I will put a sword through his righteous face.

52
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:27,090
You can't stay here.

53
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,780
He would have been a true king,

54
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:32,820
a good king.

55
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:34,750
Tell me, Ser Loras,

56
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:37,490
what do you desire most in this world?

57
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,220
Revenge.

58
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:42,380
I have always found that to be the purest of motivations,

59
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:45,200
but you won't have a chance to put your sword through Stannis,

60
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,590
not today.

61
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:49,120
You'll be cut to pieces before he sets foot on solid ground.

62
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:51,030
If it is justice that you want,

63
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:52,970
be smart about it.

64
00:06:52,970 --> 00:06:54,980
You can't avenge him from the grave.

65
00:06:57,130 --> 00:06:58,930
Bring the horses.

66
00:07:01,530 --> 00:07:02,930
Please.

67
00:07:32,450 --> 00:07:34,100
He was very handsome.

68
00:07:34,590 --> 00:07:36,420
He was, Your Grace.

69
00:07:36,570 --> 00:07:38,220
"Your Grace."

70
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:42,470
Calling yourself king doesn't make you one.

71
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:45,630
And if Renly wasn't a king, I wasn't a queen.

72
00:07:47,110 --> 00:07:48,940
Do you want to be a queen?

73
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:50,060
No.

74
00:07:52,530 --> 00:07:54,470
I want to be the queen.

75
00:08:06,590 --> 00:08:08,890
Killed? By whom?

76
00:08:08,890 --> 00:08:10,320
Accounts differ.

77
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:13,160
Most seem to implicate Catelyn Stark in some way.

78
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,800
Really? Who'd have thought?

79
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:17,440
Some say it was one of his own kingsguard,

80
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:20,190
while still others say it was Stannis himself who did it

81
00:08:20,190 --> 00:08:22,310
after negotiations went sour.

82
00:08:22,310 --> 00:08:24,260
Whomever did it, I say well done.

83
00:08:24,260 --> 00:08:25,860
It's not what Varys says.

84
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:28,710
He says Renly's army is flocking to support Stannis,

85
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:32,310
which would give Stannis superiority over us on both land and sea.

86
00:08:32,310 --> 00:08:34,660
Littlefinger says we can outspend him three to one.

87
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:37,830
And I say father raised you to have too much respect for money.

88
00:08:37,830 --> 00:08:41,460
Stannis Baratheon is coming for us sooner rather than later.

89
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:42,790
Aren't there other things you should be doing,

90
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:45,520
like sealing my daughter in a crate so you can ship her away?

91
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:46,690
She'll be safer in Dorne.

92
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:48,680
Yes, I know how concerned you are for her safety.

93
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:50,240
It so happens that I am.

94
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,940
Myrcella is a sweet, innocent girl

95
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:53,830
and I don't blame her at all for you.

96
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,350
So clever.

97
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:01,350
Aren't you always so clever with your schemes and your plots?

98
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:04,320
Schemes and plots are the same thing.

99
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,320
They are going to attack us.

100
00:09:06,330 --> 00:09:08,070
We need to be ready.

101
00:09:08,070 --> 00:09:10,210
No need to concern yourself over it.

102
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:13,840
The king is taking personal charge of siege preparations.

103
00:09:14,130 --> 00:09:17,430
May I ask specifically what the king has in mind?

104
00:09:17,430 --> 00:09:19,990
You may specifically or you may ask vaguely.

105
00:09:19,990 --> 00:09:21,750
The answer will be the same.

106
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,320
It's important that we talk about this.

107
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:35,810
It's the king's royal prerogative

108
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:39,550
to withhold sensitive information from his councilors.

109
00:09:48,410 --> 00:09:49,780
It's wildfire.

110
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:51,860
Wildfire?

111
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:56,140
You wouldn't lie to me, would you, cousin?

112
00:09:56,790 --> 00:09:58,940
- No. - That's a lie right there.

113
00:09:58,950 --> 00:10:01,650
It is not a lie. Why would I lie?

114
00:10:02,250 --> 00:10:03,520
Tell me,

115
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:07,920
if the vile allegations against my brother and sister are true,

116
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:11,990
do you think it will make Jaime more likely to kill you or less likely?

117
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:15,630
when I tell him you're fucking her, I mean.

118
00:10:15,630 --> 00:10:17,150
I'm telling you the truth.

119
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:18,750
The smart money would be on more likely.

120
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:19,960
She's making wildfire.

121
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,520
But then perhaps his own unnatural urges

122
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:23,060
will give him sympathy for yours.

123
00:10:23,070 --> 00:10:24,350
The alchemists' guild is being commissioned.

124
00:10:24,350 --> 00:10:26,250
I suppose there's only one way to find out.

125
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:28,730
They have thousands of pots already stored in their vaults.

126
00:10:28,730 --> 00:10:30,660
They are planning to launch them from the city walls

127
00:10:30,670 --> 00:10:32,980
into Stannis's ships and armies.

128
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:34,320
Please.

129
00:10:35,930 --> 00:10:37,720
When did she tell you this?

130
00:10:39,530 --> 00:10:42,040
I heard her talking with the pyromancer.

131
00:10:42,610 --> 00:10:45,840
And the other night after I left her,

132
00:10:46,370 --> 00:10:48,000
she went to meet him.

133
00:10:48,050 --> 00:10:50,910
- I swear to you. - Swear to me on what?

134
00:10:51,050 --> 00:10:53,890
- On my life. - But I don't care about your life.

135
00:10:53,890 --> 00:10:55,730
In the light of the seven,

136
00:10:55,730 --> 00:10:57,730
by all that is holy and right,

137
00:10:57,730 --> 00:11:00,410
I, Lancel Lannister, do solemnly vow...

138
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:03,960
All right, all right. Enough. Even torturing you is boring.

139
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,480
Just get out.

140
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:11,210
Oh, Lancel, tell my friend Bronn

141
00:11:11,210 --> 00:11:13,670
to please kill you if anything should happen to me.

142
00:11:14,290 --> 00:11:17,710
Please kill me if anything should happen to Lord Tyrion.

143
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:21,510
It will be my pleasure.

144
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:28,640
- Your Grace. - What is it?

145
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:31,280
- Your Grace. - I'm sorry about your brother, Your Grace.

146
00:11:31,430 --> 00:11:33,750
I wanted to let you know that people grieve for him.

147
00:11:33,750 --> 00:11:34,490
Your Grace.

148
00:11:34,490 --> 00:11:36,320
- Fools love a fool. - Your Grace.

149
00:11:36,330 --> 00:11:39,090
I grieve for him as well... for the boy he was,

150
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,600
not the man he grew to be.

151
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,070
I need to speak to you about what I saw in that cave.

152
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:43,910
I thought I made it clear to you

153
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:45,290
there'd be no need to speak to me on this matter.

154
00:11:45,290 --> 00:11:46,160
Your Grace, I...

155
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:48,570
I've never known you to need to hear a thing twice.

156
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:52,680
And I've never known you to hide from the truth.

157
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:54,010
You've come to lecture me on truth?

158
00:11:54,010 --> 00:11:55,120
I've come to tell you that what I saw...

159
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:57,830
All my brother's bannermen have come to my side.

160
00:11:59,810 --> 00:12:02,400
Except the Tyrells, who fled like cowards.

161
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,820
They won't be able to resist us now.

162
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:06,520
Soon I shall be sitting on the Iron Throne.

163
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,450
Nothing is worth what this will cost you,

164
00:12:08,450 --> 00:12:10,730
- not even the Iron... - I'll hear no more about it.

165
00:12:18,010 --> 00:12:21,160
Take a company of men, secure the perimeter.

166
00:12:22,210 --> 00:12:23,940
When do we sail for King's Landing?

167
00:12:23,990 --> 00:12:26,320
As soon as I've consolidated my troops.

168
00:12:26,690 --> 00:12:28,860
We'll make short work of the Lannisters' fleet.

169
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:30,630
Once Blackwater Bay is cleared,

170
00:12:30,630 --> 00:12:33,680
we'll deliver our troops to their doorstep and take the city.

171
00:12:34,750 --> 00:12:36,950
And will you bring Lady Melisandre with you?

172
00:12:38,370 --> 00:12:40,100
That's not your concern.

173
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:41,560
If you take king's landing

174
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:44,120
with her by your side, the victory will be hers.

175
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,810
I never thought I'd have reason to doubt your loyalty.

176
00:12:45,810 --> 00:12:47,150
Was I wrong?

177
00:12:47,170 --> 00:12:49,380
Loyal service means telling hard truths.

178
00:12:49,380 --> 00:12:50,940
Oh, truth again.

179
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,550
All right, what's the truth?

180
00:12:55,350 --> 00:12:56,780
The hard truth?

181
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:58,330
She's a foreigner

182
00:12:58,850 --> 00:13:00,990
preaching her foreign religion.

183
00:13:00,990 --> 00:13:04,980
Some believe she whispers orders in your ear and you obey.

184
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,930
What do you believe?

185
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:16,220
You won those bannermen from Renly.

186
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,990
Don't lose them to her.

187
00:13:24,270 --> 00:13:26,860
We set out for King's Landing without Lady Melisandre.

188
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:31,920
And you lead the fleet into Blackwater bay.

189
00:13:32,990 --> 00:13:34,950
Your Grace, I'm honored, but my time on the sea

190
00:13:34,950 --> 00:13:37,810
was spent evading ships, not attacking them.

191
00:13:37,810 --> 00:13:39,560
The other lords won't be happy.

192
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:42,540
Most of those lords should consider themselves lucky

193
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:44,680
I don't hang them for treason.

194
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,400
Hard truths cut both ways, Ser Davos.

195
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:09,770
I've got it! I've got it!

196
00:14:09,830 --> 00:14:12,460
So it's that one there at the top, on the right.

197
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:16,640
Buy my fruit, My Lord. Fresh fruit.

198
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,430
Stannis has more infantry,

199
00:14:18,430 --> 00:14:20,700
more ships, more horses.

200
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:22,160
What do we have?

201
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:24,580
There's that mind of yours you keep going on about.

202
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:27,680
Well, I've never actually been able to kill people with it.

203
00:14:28,170 --> 00:14:30,630
Good thing. I'd be out of a job.

204
00:14:31,550 --> 00:14:33,220
What about your father?

205
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:36,270
He hasn't sent a raven in weeks.

206
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:38,090
He's very busy.

207
00:14:38,150 --> 00:14:41,990
Being repeatedly humiliated by Robb Stark is time-consuming.

208
00:14:42,570 --> 00:14:44,560
We won't be able to hold the city against Stannis,

209
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:46,080
not the way Joffrey's planning on holding it.

210
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:48,670
Corruption, yes.

211
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:53,060
We are swollen, bloated, foul.

212
00:14:53,650 --> 00:14:56,350
Brother fornicates with sister in the bed of kings

213
00:14:56,350 --> 00:15:00,070
and we're surprised when the fruit of their incest is rotten?

214
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:03,800
Yes, a rotten king.

215
00:15:04,230 --> 00:15:06,410
It's hard to argue with his assessment.

216
00:15:06,710 --> 00:15:09,280
Not after what he did to your birthday present.

217
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:11,790
The king is a lost cause.

218
00:15:11,950 --> 00:15:14,190
It's the rest of us I'm worried about now.

219
00:15:14,290 --> 00:15:18,190
A dancing king, prancing down his bloodstained halls

220
00:15:18,190 --> 00:15:22,220
to the tune of a twisted demon monkey.

221
00:15:23,870 --> 00:15:26,070
You have to admire his imagination.

222
00:15:26,130 --> 00:15:29,560
- He's talking about you. - What?

223
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,270
Demon monkey?

224
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:33,380
People think you're pulling the king's strings.

225
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,720
They blame you for the city's ills.

226
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:38,070
Blame me? I'm trying to save them.

227
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,950
You don't need to convince me.

228
00:15:42,060 --> 00:15:43,590
Demon monkey.

229
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:15,100
Yeah, come on.

230
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,750
You're the crew of the Sea Bitch?

231
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:20,090
I'm your commander. Welcome.

232
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,020
Stop.

233
00:16:24,950 --> 00:16:26,240
Stop!

234
00:16:26,750 --> 00:16:29,350
Your Captain commands you to stop.

235
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:32,180
Where are we heading, Captain?

236
00:16:34,090 --> 00:16:37,690
The Stony Shore to raid their villages.

237
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:39,920
There'll be spoils in it for you, and women,

238
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,440
if you do your jobs well.

239
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:44,120
And who decides if we've done our jobs well?

240
00:16:45,950 --> 00:16:47,050
I do.

241
00:16:48,190 --> 00:16:49,450
Your Captain.

242
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:54,810
I have been reaving and raping

243
00:16:54,810 --> 00:16:58,260
since before you left Balon's balls, Captain.

244
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:03,030
Don't reckon I've got much use for your ideas on how to do it.

245
00:17:03,180 --> 00:17:06,310
Don't reckon I've got much use for a Captain at all.

246
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:10,080
I'm thinking I can do the job of Captain real well myself.

247
00:17:10,810 --> 00:17:13,050
All I need is a ship.

248
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:17,250
You wouldn't know where i could find myself a ship now, would you?

249
00:17:21,570 --> 00:17:22,940
You could do that,

250
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:25,200
take the ship, head out on your own.

251
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,640
And I will hunt you down,

252
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:29,570
drag you back here in chains, and hang you for a traitor.

253
00:17:29,570 --> 00:17:32,270
Stop. We yield.

254
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:38,190
Congratulations on your first command.

255
00:17:38,190 --> 00:17:41,040
Thank you. Kind of you to come see me off.

256
00:17:41,050 --> 00:17:42,790
Oh, I'm not here for you.

257
00:17:42,790 --> 00:17:44,920
I was just on my way to Red Harbor.

258
00:17:45,630 --> 00:17:49,210
I've got 30 ships. There's nowhere to put them here.

259
00:17:49,270 --> 00:17:50,910
Too narrow.

260
00:17:51,110 --> 00:17:52,820
You'd better get out there.

261
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,850
Wouldn't want them to set sail without you.

262
00:17:54,850 --> 00:17:56,570
That would never happen.

263
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:59,740
My crew would wait on deck for a year if I asked them to.

264
00:18:00,910 --> 00:18:02,510
This lot, though...

265
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:06,220
Enjoy the Stony Shore.

266
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:13,980
Come on, I'll take you out.

267
00:18:14,550 --> 00:18:15,900
Who are you?

268
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:17,820
Dagmer, your first mate.

269
00:18:19,230 --> 00:18:20,900
Why aren't you with the rest of them?

270
00:18:21,550 --> 00:18:23,160
Or did they send you to

271
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:25,560
row me out and dump me halfway in the sea?

272
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,860
That would be good for a laugh.

273
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:29,720
They're not gonna respect you until you prove yourself.

274
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:30,960
And how am I supposed to prove

275
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,210
myself by pillaging piss-poor fishing villages?

276
00:18:33,210 --> 00:18:34,550
You're not.

277
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,570
And yet that's the task my father has given me

278
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:40,260
to prove that I'm a true Iron Islander.

279
00:18:41,010 --> 00:18:42,850
They're all Iron Islanders.

280
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:46,790
Do they do as they're told or do they do as they like?

281
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:56,280
The Stony Shore's not far from Torrhen's Square.

282
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:59,480
The seat of the House of Tallhart...

283
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:02,220
a more impressive prize than a few fishermen's daughters.

284
00:19:04,470 --> 00:19:07,030
- What, you don't think we could take it? - No, we could.

285
00:19:07,030 --> 00:19:08,980
We could never hold it for more than a few days.

286
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:11,470
As soon as Winterfell got word that we'd taken Torrhen's Square,

287
00:19:11,470 --> 00:19:14,020
the Starks would send their men to take it back.

288
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:17,140
And then...

289
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:25,690
Take me to my ship.

290
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:32,720
The Starks have overextended their lines.

291
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:34,810
Now that summer's over,

292
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:37,010
they'll have a hard time keeping their men and horses fed.

293
00:19:37,010 --> 00:19:39,440
The Starks understand winter better than we ever will.

294
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:41,000
The cold won't beat them.

295
00:19:41,110 --> 00:19:45,530
Our spies report growing discontent among the northern lords.

296
00:19:45,910 --> 00:19:50,450
They want to return home and gather the harvest before the crops turn.

297
00:19:50,450 --> 00:19:53,330
And I'm sure if those same spies snuck into our own encampments,

298
00:19:53,330 --> 00:19:56,700
they would report growing discontent amongst the southern lords.

299
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:58,970
This is war; no one's content.

300
00:20:01,690 --> 00:20:04,480
We've underestimated the Stark boy for too long.

301
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:07,790
He has a good mind for warfare, his men worship him.

302
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:09,890
And as long as he keeps winning battles,

303
00:20:09,890 --> 00:20:12,580
they'll keep believing he is King in the North.

304
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:15,600
You've been waiting for him to fail.

305
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:17,880
He is not going to fail,

306
00:20:18,290 --> 00:20:20,040
not without our help.

307
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:24,930
So how do we stop him?

308
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:27,040
We've worked through the night, My Lord.

309
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:29,660
Perhaps we'd profit from some sleep.

310
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:31,810
As I think you would, Reginald.

311
00:20:31,810 --> 00:20:33,040
And because you're my cousin,

312
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:35,960
I might even let you wake from that sleep.

313
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:39,730
Go, I'm sure your wife must miss you.

314
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:41,370
My wife's in Lannisport.

315
00:20:41,370 --> 00:20:43,220
Well, then you'd better start riding.

316
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:48,320
Go before I change my mind and send her your head.

317
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:50,470
If your name wasn't Lannister,

318
00:20:50,470 --> 00:20:54,290
you'd be scrubbing out pots in the cook's tent. Go!

319
00:20:57,470 --> 00:20:59,580
Not wine, water.

320
00:20:59,790 --> 00:21:01,790
We'll be here for some time.

321
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:07,430
Girl.

322
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,570
Where are you from?

323
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,320
Maidenpool, My Lord.

324
00:21:13,710 --> 00:21:16,220
And who are the Lords of Maidenpool?

325
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:20,280
- Remind me. - House Mooton, My Lord.

326
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:22,050
And what is their sigil?

327
00:21:26,220 --> 00:21:28,110
A red salmon.

328
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:31,120
I think a Maidenpool girl would remember that.

329
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:34,840
You're a northerner, aren't you?

330
00:21:35,710 --> 00:21:38,820
Good. One more time, where are you from?

331
00:21:39,030 --> 00:21:42,080
Barrowton, My Lord. House Dustin.

332
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:46,020
Two crossed longaxes beneath a black crown.

333
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:51,410
And what do they say of Robb Stark in the north?

334
00:21:54,090 --> 00:21:55,880
They call him the young wolf.

335
00:21:56,710 --> 00:21:57,860
And?

336
00:21:59,030 --> 00:22:02,190
They say he rides into battle on the back of a giant direwolf.

337
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:07,000
They say he can turn into a wolf himself when he wants.

338
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:10,260
They say he can't be killed.

339
00:22:11,450 --> 00:22:13,150
And do you believe them?

340
00:22:14,060 --> 00:22:16,120
No, My Lord.

341
00:22:16,970 --> 00:22:18,820
Anyone can be killed.

342
00:22:26,730 --> 00:22:28,350
Fetch that water.

343
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:10,830
A girl says nothing.

344
00:23:14,250 --> 00:23:16,770
A girl keeps her mouth closed.

345
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:19,000
No one hears,

346
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:22,690
and friends may talk in secret, yes?

347
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,860
A boy becomes a girl.

348
00:23:29,070 --> 00:23:30,300
I was always a girl.

349
00:23:30,300 --> 00:23:31,870
And I was always aware.

350
00:23:32,990 --> 00:23:35,040
But the girl keeps secrets.

351
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:38,180
It is not for a man to spoil them.

352
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:42,160
You're one of them now.

353
00:23:44,490 --> 00:23:46,240
I should have let you burn.

354
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:52,180
And you fetch water for one of them now.

355
00:23:52,780 --> 00:23:55,040
Why is this right for you and wrong for me?

356
00:23:56,510 --> 00:23:57,740
I didn't have a choice.

357
00:23:57,740 --> 00:24:00,960
You did. I did.

358
00:24:02,100 --> 00:24:03,590
And here we are.

359
00:24:06,770 --> 00:24:08,570
A man pays his debts.

360
00:24:08,970 --> 00:24:10,800
A man owes three.

361
00:24:10,910 --> 00:24:12,390
Three what?

362
00:24:13,330 --> 00:24:16,500
The red god takes what is his, lovely girl.

363
00:24:16,940 --> 00:24:19,580
And only death may pay for life.

364
00:24:20,870 --> 00:24:23,410
You saved me and the two I was with.

365
00:24:23,580 --> 00:24:26,350
You stole three deaths from the red god.

366
00:24:30,030 --> 00:24:31,680
We have to give them back.

367
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:36,860
Speak three names

368
00:24:37,870 --> 00:24:39,880
and the man will do the rest.

369
00:24:42,190 --> 00:24:43,840
Three lives I will give you--

370
00:24:43,840 --> 00:24:46,800
no more, no less, and we're done.

371
00:24:47,350 --> 00:24:48,980
I can name anyone

372
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:51,650
and you'll kill him?

373
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:54,730
A man has said.

374
00:24:57,980 --> 00:24:59,600
The one who tortures everyone.

375
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:01,050
A man needs a name.

376
00:25:01,050 --> 00:25:02,820
I don't know his name.

377
00:25:03,420 --> 00:25:04,930
They call him the Tickler.

378
00:25:04,930 --> 00:25:06,650
That is enough.

379
00:25:07,780 --> 00:25:11,360
Go now, girl. Your master is thirsty.

380
00:25:25,150 --> 00:25:26,440
He's not here yet.

381
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:28,830
He'd have seen us, blown the horn.

382
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:30,390
When will he come?

383
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:33,080
The Halfhand does things in his own time.

384
00:25:33,290 --> 00:25:35,430
My uncle told me stories about him.

385
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:37,320
Most of them are true.

386
00:25:37,330 --> 00:25:40,630
I heard the Halfhand spent half of last winter beyond the wall.

387
00:25:40,670 --> 00:25:41,930
The whole winter.

388
00:25:41,930 --> 00:25:44,510
He was north of the Skirling Pass when the snows came.

389
00:25:44,510 --> 00:25:46,110
Had to wait for the thaw.

390
00:25:46,540 --> 00:25:50,100
So it is possible for someone to survive out here on their own.

391
00:25:50,490 --> 00:25:53,410
Well, possible for the Halfhand.

392
00:25:53,500 --> 00:25:55,110
Beautiful, isn't it?

393
00:25:55,760 --> 00:25:57,440
Gilly would love it here.

394
00:25:58,340 --> 00:26:01,470
There's nothing more sickening than a man in love.

395
00:26:29,050 --> 00:26:30,810
About time you did something.

396
00:26:32,310 --> 00:26:33,860
At least you'll keep warm.

397
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:37,560
The Fist of the First Men.

398
00:26:38,850 --> 00:26:41,080
Think of how old this place is--

399
00:26:42,190 --> 00:26:44,680
before the Targaryens defeated the Andals,

400
00:26:44,680 --> 00:26:47,370
before the Andals took Westeros from the first men.

401
00:26:47,370 --> 00:26:50,410
Before I die, please, stop talking.

402
00:26:50,920 --> 00:26:52,830
Thousands and thousands of years ago,

403
00:26:52,830 --> 00:26:55,930
the first men stood here where we're standing

404
00:26:55,950 --> 00:26:57,790
all through the long night.

405
00:27:00,350 --> 00:27:02,690
What do you think they were like, the first men?

406
00:27:02,730 --> 00:27:04,220
Stupid.

407
00:27:04,310 --> 00:27:07,660
Smart people don't find themselves in places like this.

408
00:27:07,830 --> 00:27:09,500
I think they were afraid.

409
00:27:11,810 --> 00:27:14,330
I think they came here to get away from something.

410
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:17,270
And I don't think it worked.

411
00:27:22,100 --> 00:27:23,460
Wildlings?

412
00:27:25,860 --> 00:27:27,990
One blast is for rangers returning.

413
00:27:27,990 --> 00:27:29,770
Wildlings is two blasts.

414
00:27:29,940 --> 00:27:32,910
So you got to stand there waiting,

415
00:27:33,670 --> 00:27:35,210
wondering.

416
00:27:35,330 --> 00:27:37,190
One blast for friends,

417
00:27:38,280 --> 00:27:39,940
two for foes.

418
00:27:42,120 --> 00:27:44,460
And three for white walkers.

419
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:49,150
It's been 1,000 years,

420
00:27:49,150 --> 00:27:52,400
but that's the only time they blow the horn three times.

421
00:27:52,670 --> 00:27:55,150
But if it's been 1,000 years, how do you know?

422
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:58,690
- Well... -  I read in a book.

423
00:27:59,700 --> 00:28:00,870
Look.

424
00:28:02,690 --> 00:28:04,240
It's Qhorin Halfhand.

425
00:28:04,540 --> 00:28:07,760
Aye, we'll live another day.

426
00:28:08,580 --> 00:28:10,150
Hurrah.

427
00:28:19,650 --> 00:28:21,710
Take care, My Lord.

428
00:28:22,660 --> 00:28:25,630
I remember reading an old sailor's proverb--

429
00:28:25,740 --> 00:28:28,280
"Piss on wildfire and your cock burns off."

430
00:28:28,280 --> 00:28:32,280
Oh, I have not conducted this experiment.

431
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:34,370
It could well be true.

432
00:28:34,370 --> 00:28:36,490
The substance burns so hot,

433
00:28:36,490 --> 00:28:39,710
it melts wood, stone, even steel,

434
00:28:39,710 --> 00:28:42,600
and, of course, flesh.

435
00:28:43,130 --> 00:28:47,830
The substance burns so hot, it melts flesh like tallow.

436
00:28:50,840 --> 00:28:54,010
After the dragons died, wildfire was the key

437
00:28:54,010 --> 00:28:56,410
to the Targaryen power.

438
00:28:57,610 --> 00:28:59,440
My companion takes issue.

439
00:28:59,470 --> 00:29:01,350
If I could tell you how many crazy old men

440
00:29:01,350 --> 00:29:03,830
I've seen pushing carts around army camps

441
00:29:03,830 --> 00:29:06,990
making grand claims about jars full of pig shit...

442
00:29:07,420 --> 00:29:08,150
No offense meant.

443
00:29:08,150 --> 00:29:10,840
Our order does not deal in pig shit.

444
00:29:10,840 --> 00:29:13,540
The substance is fire given form.

445
00:29:13,540 --> 00:29:16,710
And we have been perfecting it since the days of Maegor.

446
00:29:16,710 --> 00:29:17,750
To do what?

447
00:29:17,750 --> 00:29:22,000
The jars are put in catapults and flung at the enemy.

448
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:23,650
How much do you have?

449
00:29:28,090 --> 00:29:31,380
If you could get real soldiers to man the catapults,

450
00:29:31,380 --> 00:29:34,720
then maybe you'd hit your target one time in 10,

451
00:29:34,830 --> 00:29:38,190
but all the real soldiers are in the Riverlands with your father.

452
00:29:38,190 --> 00:29:40,210
My Lord, this man is insulting.

453
00:29:40,210 --> 00:29:42,360
I don't know if you've ever seen a battle, old man,

454
00:29:42,360 --> 00:29:43,980
but things can get a bit messy.

455
00:29:43,980 --> 00:29:46,020
'cause when we're flinging things at Stannis,

456
00:29:46,020 --> 00:29:47,560
he's flinging them right back at us.

457
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:50,590
Men die, men shit themselves, men run,

458
00:29:50,590 --> 00:29:52,340
which means pots falling,

459
00:29:52,340 --> 00:29:54,200
which means fire inside the walls,

460
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:56,290
which means the poor cunts trying to defend the city

461
00:29:56,290 --> 00:29:58,590
end up burning it down.

462
00:29:59,280 --> 00:30:01,300
My friend remains unconvinced.

463
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:03,610
He would not dare insult my order

464
00:30:03,610 --> 00:30:05,330
whilst Aerys Targaryen lived.

465
00:30:05,330 --> 00:30:08,190
Well, he's not living anymore.

466
00:30:08,190 --> 00:30:11,130
And all his pots of wildfire didn't help him, did they?

467
00:30:11,700 --> 00:30:14,730
Men win wars, not magic tricks.

468
00:30:30,530 --> 00:30:34,690
We have been working tirelessly day and night

469
00:30:34,690 --> 00:30:39,190
ever since your royal sister commanded us to do so.

470
00:30:39,190 --> 00:30:41,470
Our present count stands

471
00:30:41,470 --> 00:30:44,990
at 7,811,

472
00:30:45,210 --> 00:30:50,510
Enough to burn Stannis Baratheon's fleet and armies both.

473
00:30:50,510 --> 00:30:52,660
This is a shit idea.

474
00:30:53,190 --> 00:30:56,770
I'm afraid I have to concur with my advisor, Wisdom Hallyne.

475
00:30:57,600 --> 00:31:01,310
The contents of this room could lay King's Landing low.

476
00:31:02,990 --> 00:31:06,700
You won't be making wildfire for my sister any longer.

477
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:10,740
You'll be making it for me.

478
00:31:20,560 --> 00:31:22,110
Dracarys.

479
00:31:29,860 --> 00:31:31,900
Dracarys.

480
00:31:41,460 --> 00:31:43,870
He'll be able to feed himself from now on.

481
00:31:48,270 --> 00:31:50,540
Let him sleep, Doreah.

482
00:31:50,540 --> 00:31:52,160
Yes, Khaleesi.

483
00:31:54,870 --> 00:31:56,190
He loves you.

484
00:32:08,150 --> 00:32:09,930
Thank you, my friend.

485
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:15,020
Did you see the dress Xaro had made for you?

486
00:32:15,980 --> 00:32:18,490
They say he's the wealthiest man in Qarth.

487
00:32:18,800 --> 00:32:20,000
It is known.

488
00:32:20,970 --> 00:32:24,010
And if Qarth is the wealthiest city in Essos--

489
00:32:24,010 --> 00:32:25,990
The last time a rich man gave me a dress,

490
00:32:25,990 --> 00:32:27,860
he was selling me to Khal Drogo.

491
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:37,500
Xaro is our host, but we know nothing about him.

492
00:32:38,600 --> 00:32:40,420
Men like to talk about other men

493
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:42,560
when they're happy.

494
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:52,510
You would look like a real princess in Xaro's...

495
00:32:52,510 --> 00:32:54,820
She's not a princess. She's a Khaleesi.

496
00:33:01,710 --> 00:33:03,980
You should wear it, khaleesi.

497
00:33:03,980 --> 00:33:05,380
You are their guest.

498
00:33:05,380 --> 00:33:07,400
It would be rude not to.

499
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:31,180
And you must visit the night market.

500
00:33:31,180 --> 00:33:32,580
The Qartheen night market

501
00:33:32,580 --> 00:33:35,020
is like no night market you've ever seen.

502
00:33:35,320 --> 00:33:36,750
It sounds wonderful.

503
00:33:36,750 --> 00:33:39,170
The Meereens think they have a night market.

504
00:33:39,420 --> 00:33:41,300
I will take you there myself.

505
00:33:41,690 --> 00:33:43,910
Please excuse me for a moment.

506
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:49,490
What are they doing?

507
00:33:49,490 --> 00:33:52,630
Malakko says the statue is too heavy to carry.

508
00:33:53,140 --> 00:33:55,040
Kovarro says that Malakko is an idiot.

509
00:33:55,040 --> 00:33:57,570
They can pry out the gems, the rest is pure gold.

510
00:33:57,570 --> 00:34:01,110
Very soft. He can chop off as much as we can carry.

511
00:34:28,930 --> 00:34:31,470
My brother used to say the only thing the Dothraki knew how to do

512
00:34:31,470 --> 00:34:33,420
was steal things better men have built.

513
00:34:33,710 --> 00:34:34,860
It's not the only thing.

514
00:34:35,260 --> 00:34:37,290
They're quite good at killing the better men.

515
00:34:37,720 --> 00:34:39,770
That's not the kind of queen I'm going to be.

516
00:34:39,770 --> 00:34:41,500
Mother of dragons.

517
00:34:43,370 --> 00:34:45,660
On behalf of the warlocks of Qarth,

518
00:34:45,660 --> 00:34:47,110
I welcome you.

519
00:34:49,010 --> 00:34:50,230
A demonstration?

520
00:34:52,950 --> 00:34:56,060
Take this gem. Look at it.

521
00:34:57,220 --> 00:34:58,780
Into its depths.

522
00:35:00,070 --> 00:35:01,720
So many facets.

523
00:35:02,580 --> 00:35:06,250
Look closely enough and you can see yourself in them.

524
00:35:08,670 --> 00:35:10,400
Often more than once.

525
00:35:14,200 --> 00:35:17,710
Should you grow tired of Xaro's baubles and trinkets,

526
00:35:17,710 --> 00:35:20,680
it would be an honor to host you at the House of the Undying.

527
00:35:21,950 --> 00:35:23,540
You're always welcome,

528
00:35:23,540 --> 00:35:25,240
Mother of Dragons.

529
00:35:32,970 --> 00:35:34,730
My apologies.

530
00:35:35,040 --> 00:35:37,100
Pyat Pree is one of the Thirteen.

531
00:35:37,100 --> 00:35:40,160
It was customary for me to extend him an invitation.

532
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:43,280
Customs die slow deaths in Qarth.

533
00:35:43,460 --> 00:35:45,910
What is the House of the Undying?

534
00:35:45,910 --> 00:35:49,740
It is where the warlocks go to squint at dusty books

535
00:35:49,740 --> 00:35:51,350
and drink shade of the evening.

536
00:35:51,350 --> 00:35:55,300
It turns their lips blue and their minds soft...

537
00:35:55,300 --> 00:36:00,300
So soft, they actually believe their parlor tricks are magic.

538
00:36:04,390 --> 00:36:06,180
You watch over her.

539
00:36:09,090 --> 00:36:10,390
Do I know you?

540
00:36:10,390 --> 00:36:11,900
I know you.

541
00:36:12,350 --> 00:36:14,820
Jorah Mormont of Bear Island.

542
00:36:15,940 --> 00:36:17,310
Who are you?

543
00:36:17,980 --> 00:36:19,000
I'm no one.

544
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:22,120
But she is the Mother of Dragons.

545
00:36:22,310 --> 00:36:25,210
She needs true protectors now more than ever.

546
00:36:26,040 --> 00:36:27,410
They shall come day and night

547
00:36:27,410 --> 00:36:29,820
to see the wonder born into the world again.

548
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:33,230
And when they see, they shall lust,

549
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:36,860
for dragons are fire made flesh.

550
00:36:37,430 --> 00:36:40,050
And fire is power.

551
00:36:50,370 --> 00:36:51,960
It looked like Stannis.

552
00:36:53,570 --> 00:36:55,780
To me it just looked like...

553
00:36:59,630 --> 00:37:01,710
a shadow in the shape of a man.

554
00:37:02,130 --> 00:37:03,850
In the shape of stannis.

555
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:11,660
We should reach my son's camp tomorrow.

556
00:37:11,660 --> 00:37:13,480
Will you stay there long, My Lady?

557
00:37:13,480 --> 00:37:16,550
Only long enough to tell Robb what I have seen.

558
00:37:17,410 --> 00:37:20,120
After that, I will leave for Winterfell.

559
00:37:21,970 --> 00:37:23,770
My two youngest need me.

560
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:26,910
I've been away from them for far too long.

561
00:37:27,950 --> 00:37:29,530
I never knew my mother.

562
00:37:31,190 --> 00:37:32,560
I'm sorry.

563
00:37:33,550 --> 00:37:35,640
My own mother died on the birthing bed

564
00:37:37,180 --> 00:37:38,900
when I was very young.

565
00:37:42,370 --> 00:37:44,050
It's a bloody business.

566
00:37:45,030 --> 00:37:48,090
What comes after is even harder.

567
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:52,260
Once you're safely back amongst your own people,

568
00:37:53,650 --> 00:37:55,760
will you give me leave to go, My Lady?

569
00:37:56,610 --> 00:37:58,310
You mean to kill Stannis.

570
00:37:58,900 --> 00:38:00,280
I swore a vow.

571
00:38:00,280 --> 00:38:03,110
But Stannis has a great army around him.

572
00:38:03,640 --> 00:38:06,260
His own guards are sworn to keep him safe.

573
00:38:06,260 --> 00:38:07,990
I'm as good as any of them.

574
00:38:09,670 --> 00:38:11,390
I should never have fled.

575
00:38:11,390 --> 00:38:14,060
Renly's death was no fault of yours.

576
00:38:14,610 --> 00:38:16,290
You served him bravely.

577
00:38:17,590 --> 00:38:19,510
I only held him that once

578
00:38:21,080 --> 00:38:22,630
as he was dying.

579
00:38:25,880 --> 00:38:27,450
He's gone, Brienne.

580
00:38:28,340 --> 00:38:30,490
You serve nothing and no one

581
00:38:30,490 --> 00:38:32,110
by following him into the earth.

582
00:38:33,080 --> 00:38:35,600
Renly's enemies are Robb's enemies as well.

583
00:38:41,180 --> 00:38:43,020
I do not know your son, My Lady...

584
00:38:45,340 --> 00:38:49,080
But I could serve you if you would have me.

585
00:38:49,860 --> 00:38:51,260
You have courage.

586
00:38:52,170 --> 00:38:53,860
Not battle courage, perhaps,

587
00:38:53,860 --> 00:38:56,180
but, I don't know,

588
00:38:57,410 --> 00:38:59,330
a woman's kind of courage.

589
00:38:59,720 --> 00:39:01,950
And I think that when the time comes,

590
00:39:01,950 --> 00:39:03,340
you will not hold me back.

591
00:39:03,340 --> 00:39:07,400
Promise me that you will not hold me back from Stannis.

592
00:39:13,060 --> 00:39:16,050
When the time comes, I will not hold you back.

593
00:39:23,080 --> 00:39:25,060
Then I am yours, My Lady.

594
00:39:26,410 --> 00:39:27,940
I will shield your back

595
00:39:27,940 --> 00:39:30,240
and give my life for yours if it comes to that.

596
00:39:31,080 --> 00:39:34,000
I swear it by the old gods and the new.

597
00:39:41,430 --> 00:39:43,650
I vow that you shall always

598
00:39:43,650 --> 00:39:47,090
have a place in my home and at my table

599
00:39:47,190 --> 00:39:49,520
and that I shall ask no service of you

600
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:51,390
that might bring you dishonor.

601
00:39:52,150 --> 00:39:55,460
I swear it by the old gods and the new.

602
00:39:58,540 --> 00:40:01,400
And it's not just thieves, My Lord.

603
00:40:01,970 --> 00:40:03,790
There's wolves in them hills now,

604
00:40:03,810 --> 00:40:05,650
more than I've ever seen.

605
00:40:06,510 --> 00:40:09,580
They come down in the night and they kill my sheep.

606
00:40:09,950 --> 00:40:11,410
My three sons is away

607
00:40:11,410 --> 00:40:13,360
fighting for your brother, My Lord.

608
00:40:13,360 --> 00:40:15,770
They'll fight, keep fighting

609
00:40:15,770 --> 00:40:17,500
till they're told to go home.

610
00:40:17,500 --> 00:40:19,940
I have no one to man my flock now. Only me.

611
00:40:21,600 --> 00:40:24,530
I can't keep watch all day and all night.

612
00:40:25,970 --> 00:40:28,760
We can send two orphan boys from Winterstown home with you

613
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:30,600
to help watch over your flock,

614
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:32,500
if you can give them room and board.

615
00:40:32,500 --> 00:40:34,970
My wife always prayed for more children.

616
00:40:35,260 --> 00:40:37,820
We'll look after them. Thank you, My Lord.

617
00:40:37,820 --> 00:40:40,250
And may the gods bless you and yours.

618
00:40:43,580 --> 00:40:44,970
Stop it.

619
00:40:46,680 --> 00:40:49,350
If that's everyone, I'm going to go for a ride before dark.

620
00:40:49,350 --> 00:40:50,220
Good.

621
00:40:50,560 --> 00:40:51,530
Hodor.

622
00:40:51,530 --> 00:40:52,150
Hodor.

623
00:40:52,150 --> 00:40:54,830
Bran... Lord Stark

624
00:40:54,830 --> 00:40:57,090
Torrhen's Square is under siege.

625
00:40:57,090 --> 00:40:59,840
Torrhen's Square is barely 40 leagues from here.

626
00:41:00,070 --> 00:41:02,850
How can the Lannisters strike so far north?

627
00:41:03,230 --> 00:41:05,310
Might be a raiding party led by the Mountain.

628
00:41:05,770 --> 00:41:07,880
Might be sellswords paid by Tywin Lannister.

629
00:41:07,880 --> 00:41:09,020
We have to help them.

630
00:41:09,020 --> 00:41:10,880
Most of the fighting men are away with Robb,

631
00:41:10,880 --> 00:41:12,480
but I can gather 200 decent men.

632
00:41:12,480 --> 00:41:13,800
Do you need so many?

633
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:15,600
If we can't protect our own bannermen,

634
00:41:15,600 --> 00:41:17,400
why should they protect us?

635
00:41:18,200 --> 00:41:20,760
Go, Ser Rodrik. Take the men you need.

636
00:41:20,760 --> 00:41:22,140
Won't take long, My Lord.

637
00:41:22,140 --> 00:41:24,100
Southerners don't do well up here.

638
00:41:35,010 --> 00:41:37,010
So, what does it mean?

639
00:41:37,010 --> 00:41:38,370
Ask your Maester Luwin.

640
00:41:38,370 --> 00:41:40,500
He's the one studying books all the time.

641
00:41:40,500 --> 00:41:43,910
I did ask him. He'd never heard of a three-eyed raven.

642
00:41:44,140 --> 00:41:45,890
Must not mean anything, then.

643
00:41:46,570 --> 00:41:47,460
You're lying.

644
00:41:47,460 --> 00:41:50,210
You might be a little lord, but don't you call me a liar.

645
00:41:50,690 --> 00:41:51,920
You know what it means.

646
00:41:51,920 --> 00:41:53,760
I never said I didn't.

647
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:55,720
You didn't give me an honest answer.

648
00:41:55,720 --> 00:41:58,300
That's not the same as being a liar.

649
00:41:58,300 --> 00:41:59,880
Well, it's not far off.

650
00:41:59,880 --> 00:42:03,540
So, you've been dreaming of a three-eyed raven again?

651
00:42:06,010 --> 00:42:08,400
In the Godswood, you told me you didn't dream.

652
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:10,910
Now who's a liar?

653
00:42:15,310 --> 00:42:17,140
What did you see in your dream?

654
00:42:19,550 --> 00:42:21,390
Something bad?

655
00:42:22,230 --> 00:42:23,620
Tell me, boy.

656
00:42:27,570 --> 00:42:29,820
I dreamt that the sea came to Winterfell.

657
00:42:31,640 --> 00:42:34,240
I saw waves crashing against the gates

658
00:42:35,240 --> 00:42:37,580
and the water came flowing over the walls...

659
00:42:40,300 --> 00:42:41,830
flooded the castle.

660
00:42:44,850 --> 00:42:48,560
Drowned men were floating here in the yard.

661
00:42:51,890 --> 00:42:53,710
Ser Rodrik was one of them.

662
00:42:56,940 --> 00:42:58,740
The sea is hundreds of miles away.

663
00:42:59,990 --> 00:43:00,760
I know.

664
00:43:01,710 --> 00:43:02,890
It's just a stupid dream.

665
00:43:02,890 --> 00:43:04,530
I've got to get these potatoes to the kitchen,

666
00:43:04,530 --> 00:43:06,280
or else they'll put me in chains again.

667
00:43:06,460 --> 00:43:07,310
Osha.

668
00:43:08,570 --> 00:43:09,930
The three-eyed raven,

669
00:43:11,350 --> 00:43:14,880
what do they say about it north of the Wall?

670
00:43:16,560 --> 00:43:19,310
They say all sorts of crazy things north of the Wall.

671
00:43:30,660 --> 00:43:31,540
There.

672
00:43:32,230 --> 00:43:33,230
Where?

673
00:43:33,230 --> 00:43:34,590
On that mountain.

674
00:43:35,730 --> 00:43:37,460
I don't see very well.

675
00:43:38,050 --> 00:43:38,710
A fire.

676
00:43:41,850 --> 00:43:43,200
There's a fire.

677
00:43:44,460 --> 00:43:47,270
The people sitting around it have better eyes than yours or mine.

678
00:43:47,980 --> 00:43:50,770
When they see us coming, that fire becomes a signal.

679
00:43:50,950 --> 00:43:52,750
Gives Mance Rayder plenty of time

680
00:43:52,750 --> 00:43:54,190
to throw a party in our honor.

681
00:43:54,780 --> 00:43:56,640
How many wildlings have joined him?

682
00:43:56,640 --> 00:44:00,210
From what we can tell, all of them.

683
00:44:04,820 --> 00:44:07,710
Mance has gathered them all like deer against the wolves.

684
00:44:07,710 --> 00:44:09,610
They're almost ready to make their move.

685
00:44:10,770 --> 00:44:11,430
Where?

686
00:44:11,430 --> 00:44:12,860
Somewhere safe.

687
00:44:13,360 --> 00:44:14,770
Somewhere south.

688
00:44:15,340 --> 00:44:17,530
Can't just march into their midst.

689
00:44:18,440 --> 00:44:19,520
And we can't wait for them here

690
00:44:19,520 --> 00:44:22,080
with nothing but a pile of stones to protect us.

691
00:44:22,670 --> 00:44:24,660
You saying we should fall back to the wall?

692
00:44:25,560 --> 00:44:28,050
Mance was one of us once.

693
00:44:28,690 --> 00:44:30,200
Now he's one of them.

694
00:44:30,910 --> 00:44:33,410
He's gonna teach them our way of doing things.

695
00:44:33,830 --> 00:44:35,500
They'll hit us in force.

696
00:44:35,500 --> 00:44:37,610
And they won't run away when we hit back.

697
00:44:37,850 --> 00:44:39,790
They're gonna be more organized than before,

698
00:44:40,140 --> 00:44:41,480
more disciplined,

699
00:44:42,490 --> 00:44:44,010
more like us.

700
00:44:44,550 --> 00:44:46,660
So we need to be more like them,

701
00:44:47,170 --> 00:44:48,630
do things their way.

702
00:44:49,390 --> 00:44:52,050
Sneak in, kill Mance,

703
00:44:52,050 --> 00:44:53,670
and scatter them to the winds

704
00:44:53,670 --> 00:44:55,440
before they can march on the Wall.

705
00:44:56,010 --> 00:44:58,910
- And to do that... - We need to get rid of those lookouts.

706
00:44:58,910 --> 00:45:00,960
It's not a job for 400 men.

707
00:45:01,410 --> 00:45:04,160
I need to move fast and silent.

708
00:45:04,700 --> 00:45:07,990
Harker, Stonesnake, Borba.

709
00:45:09,170 --> 00:45:12,150
Lord Commander, I'd like to join Lord Qhorin.

710
00:45:12,840 --> 00:45:14,310
I've been called lots of things,

711
00:45:14,310 --> 00:45:16,870
but that might be my first Lord Qhorin.

712
00:45:17,560 --> 00:45:19,940
You're a steward, Snow, not a ranger.

713
00:45:19,940 --> 00:45:21,680
I've fought and killed a wight.

714
00:45:21,860 --> 00:45:23,840
How many rangers can say that?

715
00:45:23,840 --> 00:45:25,120
He's the one?

716
00:45:27,400 --> 00:45:29,960
Aye. You killed a wight.

717
00:45:29,960 --> 00:45:34,120
You also let an old man beat you bloody and take your sword.

718
00:45:35,760 --> 00:45:36,660
Craster?

719
00:45:36,860 --> 00:45:39,560
In the boy's defense, that's a tough old goat.

720
00:45:42,920 --> 00:45:45,550
I could take up Jon's duties while he's gone, My Lord.

721
00:45:46,640 --> 00:45:48,170
It would be no trouble.

722
00:45:56,390 --> 00:46:00,020
Well, I hope you make a better ranger

723
00:46:00,270 --> 00:46:01,920
than you do a steward.

724
00:46:03,820 --> 00:46:04,760
Go on.

725
00:46:12,670 --> 00:46:14,390
So, tell me,

726
00:46:14,390 --> 00:46:17,700
how long has your manservant been in love with you?

727
00:46:17,880 --> 00:46:21,340
He's not my manservant and he's not in love with me.

728
00:46:21,950 --> 00:46:23,380
He's my advisor,

729
00:46:24,110 --> 00:46:25,130
my friend.

730
00:46:25,130 --> 00:46:26,590
Unlikely.

731
00:46:27,130 --> 00:46:29,870
I can almost always tell what a man wants.

732
00:46:29,870 --> 00:46:32,210
And what about what a woman wants?

733
00:46:32,210 --> 00:46:34,150
Much more complicated.

734
00:46:34,150 --> 00:46:35,380
You, for example,

735
00:46:36,500 --> 00:46:38,460
what do you want?

736
00:46:39,230 --> 00:46:41,910
To cross the narrow sea and take back the Iron Throne.

737
00:46:41,910 --> 00:46:42,680
Why?

738
00:46:43,400 --> 00:46:45,340
Because I promised my khalasar I'd protect them

739
00:46:45,340 --> 00:46:46,910
and find them a safe home.

740
00:46:47,740 --> 00:46:50,770
You want to conquer the Seven Kingdoms for the Dothraki?

741
00:46:50,770 --> 00:46:53,130
I want them because they're mine by right.

742
00:46:53,130 --> 00:46:56,060
The Iron Throne is mine and I will take it.

743
00:46:56,350 --> 00:46:58,300
Ah, a conqueror.

744
00:46:58,870 --> 00:47:00,170
And how did you get all of this?

745
00:47:00,170 --> 00:47:01,820
- Did someone give it to you? - No.

746
00:47:02,270 --> 00:47:03,510
I come from nothing.

747
00:47:03,510 --> 00:47:05,990
I hit the docks like a piece of cargo,

748
00:47:05,990 --> 00:47:08,210
except someone normally cares what happens to cargo.

749
00:47:08,210 --> 00:47:11,000
So you wanted more than you had and you took it.

750
00:47:11,400 --> 00:47:15,500
You're a conqueror, too. You're just less ambitious.

751
00:47:19,340 --> 00:47:22,390
What do you want, Xaro Xhoan Daxos?

752
00:47:23,100 --> 00:47:25,190
At the gates of the city, you bled for me.

753
00:47:25,190 --> 00:47:26,310
Why?

754
00:47:28,830 --> 00:47:30,630
I will show you why.

755
00:47:34,730 --> 00:47:37,730
The door and the vault is made of Valyrian stone.

756
00:47:38,040 --> 00:47:41,150
The hardest steel does not make a mark.

757
00:47:41,910 --> 00:47:44,840
I offered the greatest locksmiths in Qarth

758
00:47:44,840 --> 00:47:47,160
their weight in gold if they could break into it.

759
00:47:47,160 --> 00:47:49,690
I made the same offer to the greatest thieves.

760
00:47:50,300 --> 00:47:52,730
They all went home empty-handed.

761
00:47:53,020 --> 00:47:54,950
The only thing that can open this door

762
00:47:56,050 --> 00:47:57,510
is this key.

763
00:47:58,220 --> 00:47:59,670
And behind the door?

764
00:48:03,240 --> 00:48:04,810
And it can all be mine?

765
00:48:04,810 --> 00:48:05,690
All?

766
00:48:06,500 --> 00:48:08,290
Let us say half.

767
00:48:10,130 --> 00:48:14,410
More than enough to buy horses, ships, armies...

768
00:48:14,410 --> 00:48:15,780
enough to go home.

769
00:48:16,920 --> 00:48:18,800
All I have to do?

770
00:48:19,730 --> 00:48:21,080
Is marry me.

771
00:48:21,860 --> 00:48:23,860
That was a romantic proposal.

772
00:48:24,280 --> 00:48:26,370
I've already married once for love,

773
00:48:26,540 --> 00:48:28,480
but the gods stole her from me.

774
00:48:31,590 --> 00:48:33,000
I come from nothing.

775
00:48:33,500 --> 00:48:36,170
My mother and father never owned a pair of shoes.

776
00:48:36,170 --> 00:48:39,640
But marry me and I will give you the Seven Kingdoms

777
00:48:39,640 --> 00:48:43,080
and our children will be princes and princesses.

778
00:48:45,770 --> 00:48:47,010
See?

779
00:48:47,530 --> 00:48:49,760
I have more ambition than you thought.

780
00:48:51,580 --> 00:48:55,130
The time is right, Daenerys Targaryen, first of your name.

781
00:48:56,660 --> 00:48:58,640
Robert baratheon is dead.

782
00:49:05,420 --> 00:49:07,410
If you cross the sea with an army you bought--

783
00:49:07,410 --> 00:49:09,890
The Seven Kingdoms are at war with one another.

784
00:49:09,890 --> 00:49:12,550
Four false kings destroying the country.

785
00:49:12,550 --> 00:49:15,410
To win Westeros, you need support from Westeros.

786
00:49:15,410 --> 00:49:17,560
The usurper is dead.

787
00:49:17,560 --> 00:49:19,280
The Starks fight the Lannisters,

788
00:49:19,280 --> 00:49:21,160
and the Baratheons fight each other.

789
00:49:21,160 --> 00:49:22,460
According to your new friend

790
00:49:22,460 --> 00:49:24,600
who earned your trust by cutting his hand?

791
00:49:24,600 --> 00:49:27,690
The time to strike is now. We need to find ships and an army

792
00:49:27,690 --> 00:49:28,520
or we'll spend the rest of

793
00:49:28,520 --> 00:49:30,350
our lives rotting away at the edge of the world.

794
00:49:30,350 --> 00:49:33,040
Rich men do not become rich by giving more than they get.

795
00:49:33,040 --> 00:49:36,140
They'll give you ships and soldiers and they'll own you forever.

796
00:49:36,140 --> 00:49:39,240
Moving carefully is the hard way, but it's the right way.

797
00:49:39,240 --> 00:49:40,590
And if I'd listened to that advice

798
00:49:40,590 --> 00:49:43,340
outside the gates of Qarth, we'd all be dead by now.

799
00:49:43,340 --> 00:49:44,500
I know the opportunity

800
00:49:44,500 --> 00:49:47,090
before you seems like the last you'll ever have, but you must...

801
00:49:47,090 --> 00:49:49,350
Do not speak to me like I'm a child.

802
00:49:52,730 --> 00:49:53,410
I only want...

803
00:49:53,410 --> 00:49:55,050
What do you want?

804
00:49:55,050 --> 00:49:56,400
Tell me.

805
00:49:57,400 --> 00:49:58,970
To see you on the Iron Throne.

806
00:49:58,970 --> 00:50:00,020
why?

807
00:50:00,380 --> 00:50:01,560
You have a good claim.

808
00:50:01,560 --> 00:50:03,990
A title. A birthright.

809
00:50:05,410 --> 00:50:07,420
But you have something more than that.

810
00:50:08,360 --> 00:50:11,830
You may cover it up and deny it, but you have a gentle heart.

811
00:50:12,440 --> 00:50:14,610
You would not only be respected and feared,

812
00:50:14,610 --> 00:50:16,120
you would be loved.

813
00:50:17,410 --> 00:50:19,410
Someone who can rule and should rule.

814
00:50:19,410 --> 00:50:20,980
Centuries come and go without

815
00:50:20,980 --> 00:50:23,070
a person like that coming into the world.

816
00:50:24,270 --> 00:50:25,620
There are times when I look at you

817
00:50:25,620 --> 00:50:28,240
and I still can't believe you're real.

818
00:50:40,620 --> 00:50:43,750
So what would you have me do as my advisor?

819
00:50:49,840 --> 00:50:51,130
Make your own way.

820
00:50:51,930 --> 00:50:54,060
Find your own ship. You only need one.

821
00:50:54,800 --> 00:50:57,870
The allies we need are in Westeros, not Qarth.

822
00:50:59,650 --> 00:51:01,190
And how do I get the ship?

823
00:51:01,970 --> 00:51:03,560
I'll find it for you.

824
00:51:04,160 --> 00:51:06,360
A sound ship with a good captain.

825
00:51:12,200 --> 00:51:13,890
I look forward to meeting him.

826
00:51:18,080 --> 00:51:19,690
Khaleesi.

827
00:51:49,940 --> 00:51:51,500
You should stand sideface.

828
00:51:52,090 --> 00:51:53,110
Sideface?

829
00:51:54,420 --> 00:51:55,980
Sideways.

830
00:51:56,370 --> 00:51:57,360
why?

831
00:51:57,530 --> 00:51:58,710
Smaller target.

832
00:52:02,010 --> 00:52:03,420
Am I fighting someone?

833
00:52:03,860 --> 00:52:05,480
You're practicing for a fight.

834
00:52:07,360 --> 00:52:08,960
You should practice right.

835
00:52:12,190 --> 00:52:13,420
Guards!

836
00:52:14,130 --> 00:52:14,970
help.

837
00:52:15,760 --> 00:52:17,080
Did you see anything?

838
00:52:19,500 --> 00:52:22,630
Go up there. Go and see where he fell from.

839
00:52:27,610 --> 00:52:28,790
Go up the back.

840
00:52:28,800 --> 00:52:29,850
That is strange.

841
00:52:37,440 --> 00:52:38,810
Move away.

842
00:52:41,330 --> 00:52:43,350
Stand back. He's dead.

